    /// One `match` rather than four, because a 114-arm `match` is a hundred lines
    /// long and five of them is five hundred lines of generated code where one
    /// would do -- and five places for a `clippy::too_many_lines` allowance to be
    /// repeated. Four one-line accessors read the tuple.
    ///
    /// `clippy::too_many_lines` is allowed rather than avoided because there is no
    /// way to avoid it: 114 arms is 116 lines. The alternative is an index into a
    /// `static` slice, which trades a lint the tool has a number for a bounds
    /// check on every call.
